   "description": "[h1][PRE-RELEASE] Train-Coupler Mod[/h1]\r\n\r\n[b]Make use of Smart Physics by linking your creations together—without merging\r\nthem into a single creation.[/b]\r\n\r\nUnlike weld-based couplers that combine everything into one creation, this mod\r\nkeeps each railcar, locomotive, or trailer as its own independent physics body.\r\nThat means better performance on Smart Physics on large multi-car trains!\r\n\r\n[h2]How to Use[/h2]\r\n\r\n[olist]\r\n[*][b]Place:[/b] Attach a [b]Train Coupler[/b] to both creations you want to link.\r\n[*][b]Align:[/b] Bring the two couplers close to each other.\r\n[*][b]Couple / Uncouple:[/b] Press [b]E[/b] on either coupler to lock them together (or disconnect them).\r\n[*][b]Logic Automation:[/b] Connect a switch, button, or logic gate to a coupler to engage or release it remotely from your driver's seat.\r\n[/olist]\r\n\r\n[h2]Features & Design Philosophy[/h2]\r\n\r\n[list]\r\n[*][b]Independent Physics Bodies:[/b] Takes full advantage of Scrap Mechanic's Smart Physics without merging creations.\r\n[*][b]Logic-Controlled:[/b] Supports logic inputs for remote coupling and uncoupling.\r\n[*][b]Vanilla+ Style:[/b] Designed to match Scrap Mechanic's aesthetic, grid scale, and balanced gameplay.\r\n[/list]\r\n\r\n[i]Note: This mod is currently in [b]Pre-Release[/b]. If you run into bugs, physics quirks, or multiplayer issues, please report them in the comments or open an issue on GitHub![/i]\r\n\r\n[h2]Bug Reports, Feedback & Feature Requests[/h2]\r\n\r\n[list]\r\n[*][b]Bug Reports & Issues:[/b] Please report bugs, crashes, or physics quirks on [url=https://github.com/Dampfwalze/Train-Coupler/issues]GitHub Issues[/url] rather than in the Workshop comments. That makes it much easier to track, reproduce, and fix problems!\r\n[*][b]Feedback & Feature Requests:[/b] General feedback, screenshots of your trains, and ideas for new features are always welcome right here in the Steam comments (or on GitHub).\r\n[/list]\r\n\r\n[h2]Open Source & Contributing[/h2]\r\nThis mod (including all Lua scripts, JSON definitions, and editable 3D models) is open source under the [b]GNU GPLv3[/b] (with Steam Workshop & Scrap Mechanic Additional Permissions).\r\n\r\n[url=https://github.com/Dampfwalze/Train-Coupler][table noborder=1][tr][td][img]https://cdn.simpleicons.org/github/white?size=48[/img][/td][td][b]View Source Code, 3D Models & Contribute on GitHub[/b][/td][/tr][/table][/url] ",
